e:["$","div",null,{"className":"hypothesis-explanation","children":"A capable agent may already work out the right approach from the sources. Preparing guidance and consulting it takes time and money. I want to find out whether these steps prevent enough mistakes to justify the effort."}]
f:["$","div",null,{"className":"hypothesis-foot","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"signal-dot"}],"The experiment is intended to answer this question. It has not answered it yet."]}]
10:["$","section",null,{"id":"example","className":"section-block","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"01"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"GUIDANCE FOR A SPECIFIC TASK"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"What would the layer tell an agent?"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"When an agent is given a task, it needs to understand how that task fits into the existing system. The layer should identify code the agent can reuse, explain which decisions constrain the change, and show where exceptions apply. The agent should be able to see the evidence behind each answer and whether it represents an approved decision, an observed pattern or a question that still needs review."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"The agent can consult the layer about a proposed approach: whether to extend an existing component, where new code belongs, or whether a change would cross a boundary the project has chosen to preserve. The answer should explain what is allowed and why, or identify the unresolved decision that needs an owner’s judgement. The agent uses those answers in its plan, which can then be checked against the relevant decisions before work proceeds."}],["$","$L16",null,{"children":["$","$L17",null,{"id":"guidance-examples","title":"See examples of the guidance an agent could receive","summary":"How this applies to change history, conflicting documentation and questions the code cannot answer.","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"NetBox is an open-source application used to document network infrastructure, including devices and their connections. It is one of the four projects in this study."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"In the first example, an agent is asked to write code that renames a device in NetBox. The layer would draw its attention to a related requirement: the change history must preserve the old name as well as the new one. It would also explain when NetBox already handles that requirement, so the agent can choose the right approach."}],["$","$L18",null,{}]]}]}]]}]
11:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"02"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE IDEA BEHIND THE LAYER"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Turn project evidence into guidance for later work"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro section-intro-wide","children":"The layer connects two cycles: one establishes the guidance; the other uses it during engineering work. Drafting and approval happen before that guidance can be used as an approved decision, but they are not repeated for every task."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guidance-cycles","id":"guidance-cycles","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"guidance-cycle","aria-labelledby":"preparation-cycle-title","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"DRAFTING & APPROVAL CYCLE"}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"preparation-cycle-title","children":"Establish and maintain the guidance"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"cycle-steps","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Find the evidence"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Read the relevant code, documentation and recorded decisions, including exceptions and conflicting examples."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Draft and verify the guidance"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Explain each proposed rule, its scope and its evidence. Check support and contradictions before owner review."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Review and release a version"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The responsible owner approves, rejects or requests changes. Only approved decisions are released as approved guidance."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"cycle-repeat","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M3 12a9 9 0 0 1 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 1 6.74 2.74L21 8","key":"v9h5vc"}],["path",{"d":"M21 3v5h-5","key":"1q7to0"}],["path",{"d":"M21 12a9 9 0 0 1-9 9 9.75 9.75 0 0 1-6.74-2.74L3 16","key":"3uifl3"}],["path",{"d":"M8 16H3v5","key":"1cv678"}]],"className":"lucide-refresh-cw","size":17,"aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Review can send a draft back for revision before a version is released."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"cycle-timing","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Initially:"}]," establish the baseline.",["$","br",null,{}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"When evidence or decisions change:"}]," recheck affected guidance and retain, revise or retire it through review."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guidance-connection","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M5 12h14","key":"1ays0h"}],["path",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7","key":"xquz4c"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-right guidance-connection-arrow","size":28,"aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"Approved guidance"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A version with its evidence, scope and exceptions."}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The same version can support many tasks."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"guidance-cycle guidance-cycle-use","aria-labelledby":"usage-cycle-title","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"USAGE CYCLE"}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"usage-cycle-title","children":"Apply the guidance to each task"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"cycle-steps","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Consult and plan"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Retrieve the relevant guidance. Identify what can be reused, what constrains the change and which exceptions may apply."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Check and carry out the approach"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Review the plan against the guidance, make the change and recheck material changes of approach."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Check the resulting work"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Assess the change against the relevant decisions and task requirements. Record objections and unresolved questions."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"cycle-repeat","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$11:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:3:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-refresh-cw","size":17,"aria-hidden":"true"}],"$L19"]}],"$L1a"]}],"$L1b"]}],"$L1c","$L1d"]}]
12:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"03"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE PROPOSED COMPARISON"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Separate the value of guidance from the value of checking its use"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"I propose giving agents the same change to make under three conditions. This would test whether preparing guidance helps by itself, and whether consulting the layer and checking the plan adds a further benefit. The pilot procedure above is my proposed starting point; the exact prompts, budgets and checks still need validation before the trial."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"comparison comparison-three","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WITHOUT THE EXTRA LAYER"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"The agent works from the sources"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"It searches the code and available documentation, works out what matters for the task, and makes the change. This represents a capable agent doing the work directly."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WITH PREPARED GUIDANCE"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"The agent receives the rules"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The layer has examined the same sources and written guidance before the task begins. The agent receives that guidance and works with it, without an interactive check by the layer."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WITH GUIDANCE AND INTERACTION"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"The agent checks its proposed actions"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The agent receives the same guidance, consults the layer about its plan and responds to checks at agreed points. The run records whether those interactions prevent mistakes or add unnecessary work."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"caption","children":"All three conditions need the same permitted evidence and comparable resources, including opportunities for review. The cost assessment will include preparing guidance and any additional checking. The two guidance conditions must use the same frozen rules, so a difference between them is not simply caused by one receiving better guidance."}]]}]
13:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","id":"method","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"04"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE EXPERIMENT, STEP BY STEP"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"How I intend to run the experiment"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"The experiment will ask agents to make the same code change with different kinds of help, then compare the work they produce and the effort it took. Here is the proposed sequence for one test."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"method-steps","aria-label":"The four steps in one experiment","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","aria-hidden":"true","children":"1"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Prepare a task with a defensible assessment"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Case preparation starts with a project rule supported by inspectable evidence and a code-change task where that rule matters. Before an agent attempts it, the reference assessment must distinguish a correct change, a real mistake and a valid exception. That assessment stays outside the agent’s workspace."}],["$","$L16",null,{"children":["$","$L17",null,{"id":"choose-case","title":"How are tasks selected and reference answers established?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Each case starts from a published requirement or decision, with its scope checked against the implementation. If the guide and code disagree, the assessment must explain the disagreement. Copying the guide is not enough."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Each case needs a valid solution and a deliberately incorrect change, with tests that distinguish them. It also needs a legitimate exception or alternative so the scoring does not demand one particular implementation. If the evidence cannot settle the answer, that part of the case remains unresolved."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The candidate projects are NetBox, Wagtail, Paperless-ngx and HTTPX. They offer different kinds of engineering decisions, but all four use Python and three use Django. They are not a representative sample of all software projects."}],["$","$L1e",null,{}]]}]}]]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","aria-hidden":"true","children":"2"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Let the layer prepare its guidance"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The layer examines the allowed project material without seeing the change task. It drafts guidance, and a separate verifier checks whether the evidence supports it. The resulting guide is saved before the task is revealed and stays unchanged during the run."}],["$","$L16",null,{"children":[["$","$L17",null,{"id":"allowed-evidence","title":"Does the layer read the documentation, or work the rule out from code?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The experiment tests those two abilities separately."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"plain-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Working it out from code."}]," The input pack excludes documents and other statements that reveal the target rule. The layer has to use the remaining code evidence, or acknowledge that the rule cannot be established."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Using documentation."}]," The declared documents are available. The assessment checks whether the layer understands their scope, preserves exceptions and notices disagreements with the code."]}]]}],"$L1f","$L20"]}],"$L21"]}]]}]]}],"$L22","$L23"]}],"$L24","$L25"]}]
14:["$","div",null,{"className":"route-footer","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"For the work completed so far and the decisions still ahead."}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/progress/","children":["Progress & findings ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$11:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","size":18}]]}]]}]
